Hello,

i now have my Miata running triple-head with one ELSA Gloria Synergy and 2 TGA2
(8bit, PowerStorm 3D30 i think) on 3 cheap 19" TFT screens. The screen on the
Gloria is quite fine, black is really black, white is bright, colors are
brilliant, sharp picture. But the image of the 2 TGA2s looks a bit strange. It
seems the monitor gets too high voltages in the analog video inputs, or maybe
it gets some DC offset. Black is grey, not really dark, and i see effects like
shadows, bit left of the real pixels, and in the background, i see light
vertical stripes. I verified this not being a sync-on-green issue, there
doesn't seem to come any sync pulses out of the green connector. I just now
played around with the sync, fixed XFree86 binary up to (hopefully) usr VESA
sync timing, but i don't know if this really is used by the card now.

Does anyone know about electrical strangeness of the TGA2 (or maybe TGA in
general) video output? PowerStorm 4D20 has the same problem, i verified this
with my other Miata.

Any hints welcome.

...Michael

