As a Bell Canada employee, I personally spent almost 20 weeks (between 1978 
and 1986) at the DEC customer education facility in Kanata (100 Herzberg 
Road). Those class rooms and labs gave me an in-depth computer education 
that was not available at any college or university at that time. My last 
week there was for PCL-11 (3 days) and CB-11 (2 days). IIRC, Ottawa-area VAX 
related training had moved to Hull, Quebec in the early 1990's.

In 1997 I discovered that many ex-Kanta instructors had moved to "Global 
Knowledge" and were working in either downtown Ottawa or Toronto.

