Hello Fellow Vintage Computer Enthusiasts,

Please forgive the intrusion but I would like to make you all aware of
the existence of the Vintage Computer Forum at
www.vintage-computer.com/vcforum.

With nearly 600 users and a wide variety of moderated topic areas
these forums have quickly become a valuable resource for the vintage
computing community on the web.

Signing up is easy and safe and requires only an email address (which
will be used only by the forums and which will never be disseminated.)

Whatever interests you it's likely you'll find someone else with
similar interests.  If for some reason you don't, please don't
hesitate to recommend a new discussion area.  Several have been added
recently based on just these types of requests.

We look forward to your visit!

Please note, I'm well aware that not everyone on Usenet likes web
forums.  Such is life.  Please don't visit if you don't think the
forums will be of interest to you.  I am simply offering a free
service to the vintage computer community and I'm trying to get the
word out.  I like to think of the forums as a compliment to Usenet and
mail lists.  Forum bashing is fine, but we've been there before. . .
;-)

