The DECUServe system would be very willing to set up such a forum, using DEC 
Notes.

If this is of interest to you, get a (free) account on DECUServe, and then 
send vmsmail to me (coy) on that system.

HOW TO:

To sign up:  just Telnet to decuserve.org, use username REGISTRATION, and 
follow the bouncing ball.
It's nice if you sign up using accurate information, and DECUServe won't 
sell it to anybody.  Oh - there's no fee,
and no requirement to be a member of any organization.

Other info:
Doing that gets you a regular account on an OpenVMS system that is superbly 
managed by volunteers.
You'll be able to use the DEC Notes software to ask questions (and help the 
community with your answers).
DEC Notes provides an "Unseen Map" to track notes you have already read.

DECUServe provides a reasonably full set of OpenVMS software, as well as 
MultiNet and PMDF.
You get an email account that benefits from excellent inbound filtering. 
You can set up a personal web page(s).
Other things too numerous to mention, in a friendly environment.  And many 
folks on DECUServe find that
it's beneficial to have a VMS account on "another" system to occasionally 
facilitate testing on their "regular" system.




