the ability to copy one drive from another without buying a $100 
packages. The internet was for DOD use only. There was no software,
you wrote your own in BASIC the worst computer language invented.

Thus it could not be too hard to see why KO made the statement.
Really until the internet opened most people didn't need a Pieces of
Crap in thier home. His replacement really blew it with not linking
up with the phone companies and coming out with an alpha/OpenVMS based
internet appliance that linked to altavista.

What the clever miss is the real missed oppertunties that DEC had on
the ground at the time QBUS systems with real OS's and a large 
collection of software.  Failure to price the kit at low prices and
advert the world that our Boxes are better, have software with years
of history became a marker for future marketing failures.


