>
>Could someone point me towards a Telnet or FTP site where I can find
>software and some coaching for this critter? 

Well, one surprise will be that the 5.25 inch floppy disks were
not 'normal format', but special Rainbow RX50 formatted disks. IIRC,
there may have been a program that you could run on a 'normal'
IBM-compatable to format a 'normal' 5.25 floppy into a Rainbow
format disk - or, maybe it would just let you read a Rainbow disk
on a regular PC.

Rainbow FAQs: http://www.classiccmp.org/rainbow/files/rainbow.faq

Using the above link I was able to find an FTP site with some
Rainbow stuff (not sure what's there):

ftp://ftp.update.uu.se/pub/rainbow/

Check out the README file at the above FTP link - looks like
some useful stuff.

Also try http://www.google.com and put in the following
search words:

    rainbow simtel dec
    rainbow software dec

Good luck!

Lee (former Rainbow owner)


